Experiment 1: Process Creation using fork(), execlp() & wait()
Course Outcome:  CO1
Aim
To write a C program to create a new process that executes a new program using the system calls fork(), execlp() and wait().
Algorithm / Theory
●	fork() creates a new process (the child) by duplicating the calling process. It returns 0 in the child, the child's PID in the parent, and a negative value on failure.
●	execlp() replaces the current process image with a new program, searching for it using the PATH environment variable.
●	wait() suspends the calling (parent) process until one of its child processes terminates, and collects its exit status.
Program
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
 
int main() {
    pid_t pid;
    int status;
 
    printf("Parent process: PID = %d\n", getpid());
    pid = fork();
 
    if (pid < 0) {
        perror("Fork failed");
        exit(1);
    } else if (pid == 0) {
        /* Child process */
        printf("Child process: PID = %d, Parent PID = %d\n",
               getpid(), getppid());
        printf("Child is executing 'ls -l' using execlp()\n");
        execlp("ls", "ls", "-l", NULL);
        /* execlp() only returns if it fails */
        perror("execlp failed");
        exit(1);
    } else {
        /* Parent process */
        wait(&status);
        printf("Parent process: Child %d has terminated\n", pid);
    }
    return 0;
}
Experiment 2: Displaying PID and PPID
Course Outcome:  CO1
Aim
To write a C program to display the Process ID (PID) and Parent Process ID (PPID) using the system calls getpid() and getppid().
Algorithm / Theory
●	Every running process is assigned a unique Process ID (PID) by the operating system.
●	getpid() returns the PID of the calling process; getppid() returns the PID of its parent.
●	After fork(), the child's PPID is the PID of the process that created it.
Program
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
 
int main() {
    pid_t pid = fork();
 
    if (pid < 0) {
        perror("Fork failed");
        return 1;
    } else if (pid == 0) {
        printf("Child  Process -> PID: %d, PPID: %d\n", getpid(), getppid());
    } else {
        wait(NULL);
        printf("Parent Process -> PID: %d, PPID: %d\n", getpid(), getppid());
    }
    return 0;
}

